# Repo files that must not be served to the public.
#
# The deploy is `netlify deploy --prod --dir=.`, which uploads the whole checkout,
# not a built subset. Verified live on 2026-08-02: /docs/OPERATIONS.md, /package.json,
# every /supabase/migrations/*.sql, all four /supabase/functions/*/index.ts, the
# /tests/*.js files and /scripts/verify-rls.mjs all returned 200. No secrets are in
# them (they read credentials from the environment), but they are a detailed map of
# the security model of a site that takes card payments, so stop serving them.
#
# Two things make these rules work, both checked against Netlify's docs rather than
# assumed:
#   1. Rules are matched top to bottom and the first match wins, so these sit above
#      the 301s below. None of the patterns overlap today, but this is the safe order.
#   2. A rule normally loses to a real file at the same path ("shadowing"). Every path
#      here IS a real file, so each rule needs the `!` force marker to win. Without the
#      `!` these lines would do nothing at all.
#
# KNOWN GAP, do not mistake this for airtight. Netlify matches redirect rules
# case-sensitively but serves files case-insensitively, both verified: the live site
# returns 200 for /DOCS/OPERATIONS.MD, and Netlify's own matcher returns no rule for
# that path. So a case variant still reaches the file, and covering every variant would
# take 2^n rules. This blocks the paths that are actually guessable and scanned for.
# The complete fix is to stop uploading these files at all, which means deploying from
# a publish directory that holds only site files instead of `--dir=.`.
/docs/*             /404.html   404!
/supabase/*         /404.html   404!
/tests/*            /404.html   404!
/scripts/*          /404.html   404!
/package.json       /404.html   404!
/package-lock.json  /404.html   404!
/netlify.toml       /404.html   404!
/node_modules/*     /404.html   404!
# Hidden files are not uploaded by the CLI today (verified: /.gitignore and
# /.superpowers/sdd/progress.md both 404 on the live site). That is a property of the
# deploy tool, not a decision this site made, so pin the ones that would hurt.
/.superpowers/*     /404.html   404!
/.env               /404.html   404!
/.gitignore         /404.html   404!

